{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/european-food-markets/audio/main-12243cd0c953.mp3","durationSec":158.16,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":4.14,"text":"Buying food at European food markets becomes easier when you know the basic layout."},{"start":5.14,"end":7.02,"text":"An open-air market has stalls outside."},{"start":7.72,"end":10.12,"text":"A covered market puts the stalls under one roof."},{"start":11.02,"end":14.08,"text":"A food hall is usually inside and often has places to sit."},{"start":15.48,"end":19.22,"text":"Any of these places may sell ingredients, ready-to-eat dishes, or both."},{"start":19.22,"end":24.92,"text":"Picture fruit in Barcelona, a warm lunch in Paris, and bread in London."},{"start":25.74,"end":28.32,"text":"First, walk around and look at the displayed price."},{"start":29.1,"end":31.9,"text":"Notice whether people order at a counter or sit at a table."},{"start":32.54,"end":35.64,"text":"These details help you know how to buy, eat, and pay."},{"start":35.64,"end":41.14,"text":"Local market cultures differ, so watch first and ask politely when you are unsure."},{"start":42.22,"end":44.58,"text":"Food may be sold by piece or by weight."},{"start":45.22,"end":48.38,"text":"For one bread roll, say, “Two of these, please,” and point."},{"start":49.08,"end":54.26,"text":"For a practice cheese order, say, “Half a kilo, please,” or ask for a smaller amount."},{"start":54.56,"end":57.56,"text":"The seller can stop when you say, “That’s enough, thank you.”"},{"start":58.32,"end":61.14,"text":"You can also ask what is local or popular."},{"start":62.1,"end":66.94,"text":"Ask for a small sample only when it seems possible; the seller may say yes or no."},{"start":68.18,"end":72,"text":"Before the seller prepares the order, check payment with “Do you take cards?”"},{"start":72.48,"end":73.62,"text":"or “Is it cash only?”"},{"start":74.2,"end":76.24,"text":"This avoids a problem after the food is ready."},{"start":76.82,"end":78.34,"text":"Allergies need clear questions."},{"start":79.08,"end":81.98,"text":"In the European Union, fourteen allergens are regulated."},{"start":83,"end":88.56,"text":"Sellers of non-prepacked food, including food at restaurant and deli counters, must provide allergen information."},{"start":89.36,"end":93.28,"text":"They may explain it aloud, and written information must be available on request."},{"start":94.26,"end":98.04,"text":"This helps, but it is not a promise that cross-contact cannot happen."},{"start":99.16,"end":102.36,"text":"A little of another food may touch the dish during preparation."},{"start":102.94,"end":108.22,"text":"Say exactly what you cannot eat, ask to see the written information, and listen to the answer."},{"start":108.74,"end":112.24,"text":"If the answer is not safe or clear enough for you, choose something else."},{"start":113.4,"end":115.34,"text":"Never guess about a serious allergy."},{"start":116.18,"end":118.34,"text":"Tipping is not one European rule."},{"start":118.92,"end":121.24,"text":"In Spain, restaurant tips are discretionary."},{"start":121.88,"end":128.02,"text":"At a tapas bar, a customer may round up the bill; at a higher-end restaurant, about 10% can be used."},{"start":128.98,"end":134.92,"text":"In France, service compris means that service is included, so an extra tip is optional."},{"start":136.34,"end":140.82,"text":"In Britain, a bill can name a discretionary or compulsory service charge."},{"start":142.12,"end":144.2,"text":"Read the words on the bill before you decide."},{"start":144.87,"end":147.06,"text":"Also ask what kind of service you received."},{"start":147.94,"end":153.34,"text":"At a simple counter, pay the stated price unless local information suggests something different."},{"start":154.16,"end":157.74,"text":"At a table, check the bill and the local custom before adding more money."}],"words":[{"text":"Buying","start":0,"end":0.4},{"text":"food","start":0.4,"end":0.66},{"text":"